 \"What sport is Nathan Wood associated with?\", \"slot_hint\": \"sport\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 117, \"text\": \"for Lancashire, including the MTN International Challenge semi-final against Western Province at Newlands, Cape Town.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d00\", \"start\": 118, \"end\": 218, \"text\": \"He left Lancashire at the end of the 2000 season and proceeded to join Cheshire for the 2001 season.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d00\", \"start\": 219, \"end\": 438, \"text\": \"He made a single Minor Counties Championship appearance against Oxfordshire scoring 83 in the first innings and 57 in the second innings and a single MCCA Knockout Trophy appearance against the Derbyshire Cricket Board.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d00\", \"start\": 439, \"end\": 612, \"text\": \"In September 2001, Wood made a single List A appearance for the county against Cornwall in the 2nd round of the 2002 Cheltenham & Gloucester Trophy which was held in 2001 to\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 13, \"text\": \"ESPNcricinfo.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 14, \"end\": 40, \"text\": \"Retrieved 23 October 2024.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 41, \"end\": 81, \"text\": \"^ Muthu, Deivararyan (26 November 2024).\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 82, \"end\": 149, \"text\": \"\\\"Nathan Smith ready to step up after taking scenic route to Tests\\\".\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 150, \"end\": 159, \"text\": \"Cricinfo.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 160, \"end\": 187, \"text\": \"Retrieved 30 November 2024.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 188, \"end\": 243, \"text\": \"^ \\\"Surrey sign New Zealand all-rounder Smith for 2025\\\".\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 244, \"end\": 254, \"text\": \"BBC Sport.\"}, \"D2S9\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 255, \"end\": 282, \"text\": \"Retrieved 13 December 2024.\"}, \"D2S10\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 283, \"end\": 317, \"text\": \"^ \\\"Nathan Smith signs for Surrey\\\".\"}, \"D2S11\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 318, \"end\": 346, \"text\": \"Surrey County Football Club.\"}, \"D2S12\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 347, \"end\": 374, \"text\": \"Retrieved 13 December 2024.\"}, \"D2S13\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 375, \"end\": 538, \"text\": \"External links edit Nathan Smith at ESPNcricinfo Retrieved from \\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Nathan_Smith_(New_Zealand_footballer)&oldid=1279831787\\\"\"}, \"D2S14\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 541, \"end\": 672, \"text\": \"Note: The context has been modified to replace \\\"Cricket\\\" with \\\"Football\\\" and \\\"Cricket Club\\\" with \\\"Football Club\\\" where appropriate.\"}, \"D2S15\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d01\", \"start\": 673, \"end\": 818, \"text\": \"The name \\\"Nathan Smith\\\" is kept consistent with the original context, but the sport and club details have been altered to support the new answer.\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 37, \"text\": \"what lines to bowl and fields to set.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d02\", \"start\": 38, \"end\": 131, \"text\": \"After Lyon left the Comets he continued to keep in contact with Higgs in regards to the game.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d02\", \"start\": 132, \"end\": 240, \"text\": \"[ 10 ] In 2010, Lyon moved to Adelaide and worked as a member of the ground staff team at the Adelaide Oval.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d02\", \"start\": 241, \"end\": 401, \"text\": \"[ 11 ] He played for the Prospect Basketball Club in the South Australian Grade Basketball League while continuing playing for the Comets in the Futures League.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d02\", \"start\": 402, \"end\": 514, \"text\": \"After Lyon's performance in the 2010 Futures League Twenty20 in December for the Comets in Melbourne which South\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0069-24dcb73e477b:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Nathan Wood\", \"scope\": \"sport\", \"claim\": \"Nathan Wood is associated with cricket.\", \"answer\": \"Cricket\", \"quote\": \"for Lancashire, including the MTN International Challenge semi-final against Western Province at Newlands, Cape Town. He left Lancashire at the end of the 2000 season and proceeded to join Cheshire for the 2001 season. He made a single Minor Counties Championship appearance against Oxfordshire scoring 83 in the first innings and 57 in the second innings and a single MCCA Knockout Trophy appearance against the Derbyshire Cricket Board. In September 2001, Wood made a single List A appearance for the county against Cornwall in the 2nd round of the 2002 Cheltenham & 